SPOILERS:

Actually, either.  You can give gold to _any_ priest/ess, whether
co-aligned or not and get some of the benefits of bribing, i.e.,
Clairvoiyance and Protection/armor class.

The other benefits of bribing (raising alignment or being cleansed)
can only come from a co-aligned priest/ess.  You can give 0 gold to
a non-coaligned priest/ess without harm, but trying this on a 
co-aligned priest/ess results in lowering alignment by one.

Also, if you have 0 gp and are in good standing, you can #chat with
a co-aligned priest/ess and get "2 bits for an ale."


